00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:08.570 align:start position:0%
Nintendo switch is a great console name  that implies a lot of things I mean what  the hell does Wii U mean anyway but  outside of one reveal trailer and a few  confirmed details we hardly know  anything about it with a ful  presentation happening this Thursday we  don't have to wait much longer to have  our questions answered so what can we  expect here are four things to keep in  mind number one  the controller the switch is a hybrid  console which means you can take it  outside or plug it into the dock to play  on your big TV at home the gamepad  itself has removable controllers called  joi cons on either side but what about  that screen in the middle reports from  bloggers Emily Rogers and Laura Kate  Dale claim it's a touchscreen given  Nintendo's history with the Wii U 3ds  and original DS touch screen  functionality only makes sense  as for the joi cons themselves  customization is another question  immature user the grumpy cat created  some alternate color schemes for the  system which do fall in line with  Nintendo's various shades of game boys  and DS's artist Ryan Sal Amanda took  this idea even further sketching out a  few possibilities for alternate joi con  shapes and button layouts it's a  brilliant idea that just can't be unseen  but also it's super unconfirmed so don't  get too attached number 2 the specs so  what about the guts of the console  ventureBeat reports that the switch uses  Nvidia's Maxwell graphics processor  rather than the manufacturers newer  Pascal technology  this means the console has just over a  teraflop of performance power making it  less powerful than the baseline ps4 or  Xbox one digital foundry went more in  depth digging into the switches CPU and  GPU speeds according to the site CPU  speeds are constant whether the console  is docked or removed this way the game  runs the same in your living room as it  does on the go the GPU however is down  clock to just 40 percent of its total  power when not plugged in earlier  digital foundry reports claim the  controller sports a 720p screen  so the graphics will stay pretty as they  eat up less GPU power number three the  price so how much are you gonna be  paying for this thing UK retailer games  seek listed the system at around two  hundred pounds or about two hundred and  fifty dollars the same price our friend  Laura Kate Dale stated would be listed  by game another UK store loser rumors  from website mobi Pickers said that  bundles will start at two hundred and  sixty dollars with a 300 dollar Mario  bundle and a three hundred and forty  dollars Zelda and pro controller bundle  also available those prices have not  been confirmed and neither has a new  Mario game for that matter but given  that we use $300 and three hundred and  fifty dollar launch units they don't  seem too outlandish number for the games  perhaps the biggest question of all is  what games the Nintendo switch will  offer Legend of Zelda breath of the wild  has been slated for a while  more recently play tonics ukulele has  been confirmed for the system along with  Dragon Quest 10 Dragon Quest eleven lego  city undercover and rime indie darling  stardew valley also has a switch version  in the works and two more indie games  seasons of heaven and the sacred hero  have also been announced the switches  debut trailer also teased skyrim NBA 2k  17 different versions of Mario Kart 8  and splatoon and what appears to be a  new Mario game but none of these have  been officially announced a third  version of Pokemon Sun and Moon titled  Pokemon stars has also been reported and  on top of all of that  a report from Eurogamer claims the  Virtual Console will be updated to  feature GameCube titles if you're  looking for a reason to visit Super  Mario Sunshine you just might get it the  Nintendo switch presentation kicks off  Thursday January 12th at 8 p.m. Pacific  11 p.m. Eastern Nintendo will be talking  specs price and launch lineup so these  questions should have solid answers will  hopefully get that March release window  narrowed down to keep an eye on GameSpot  for all the new info and look for some  hot new switch gameplay very soon
 

